# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0
"""Colour by number in large cells, made for an older player.

A picture is a grid of cells, each with a number; the palette at the
bottom has one big button per number. Pick a colour, tap its cells.
- Cells of the chosen number are tinted and their numbers bold, so they
  are easy to find; a cell of another number cannot be painted.
- Zoom with the + and - buttons and drag to scroll: one finger is enough.
- A tap paints the whole connected area of that number at once (a
  large sky is one tap); the "Клетка" mode paints one cell per tap.
- Every tap gives a short buzz; there is no timer, no score, no ads.
- Progress is saved after every cell, so a picture can wait for tomorrow;
  the program starts on the last picture, unless it is finished, and the
  gallery opens at that picture's card.

The gallery runs from easy to hard as it scrolls down: level 1 has
16x12 cells and five colours, level 2 32x24 cells, levels 3 and 4 are
paintings in 32 and 48 cells across with up to 10 and 14 colours.

Pictures: the built-in ones in /usr/local/share/b8k/paint/, and any photo
put into ~/Раскраски (JPEG or PNG), which is turned into a picture of at
most 32 cells across and 10 colours the first time it is opened.
"""
import fcntl
import hashlib
import json
import os
import struct
import sys

import gi

